# Creality patterns

## Dual connectivity

| Channel | Port | Use for |
|---------|------|---------|
| Moonraker HTTP | `7125` (fallback try `4408`) | Status, progress, temps, fans, CFS inventory, G-code (`LED_SWITCH` = CFS box LED) |
| Creality WS | `9999` | `lightSw` (toolhead LED), `pause` 0/1, `stop` 1 |

Heartbeats on Creality WS may send `ModeCode: heart_beat` — reply with literal `"ok"`.

## Curated state tree (do not dump all Klipper objects)

```
creality.0.
  info.connection / online
  info.model, firmware, …          (adapter v1+)
  state, stateKlipper, selfTestStep
  currentJob.progress, printName, remainingText, finishAt
  currentJob.filamentSlot, filamentMaterial, filamentColor   (active)
  temp.nozzleTemp|nozzleTarget|bedTemp|bedTarget
  fans.partCooling|partCoolingRpm|hotend|board|aux
  cfs.type|state|enable|temperature|humidity|light
  cfs.T1A|T1B|T1C|T1D .color|material|occupied|active
  control.light|pause|resume|stop
```

- `printNameShort`: truncate before first `.STL` / `.stl`
- Filament colors: Creality often sends `0RRGGBB` → normalize to `#RRGGBB`
- Active CFS slot: prefer `filament_inventory_manager.active_tnn` (e.g. `T1C`)
- External spool: Moonraker `filament_rack` (`color_value` / `material_type`); `currentJob.filamentSlot` = `rack` when CFS not active
- Material type codes (`000001` …): map known catalog ids to PLA / PETG / TPU

## Controls

- `control.light` → Creality WS `{ lightSw: 0|1 }` (toolhead)
- `cfs.light` → Moonraker G-code `LED_SWITCH SWITCH=0|1` (CFS box)
- `control.pause` / `resume` / `stop` → buttons (pulse true → action → reset false)
  - pause: `{ pause: 1 }`, resume: `{ pause: 0 }`, stop: `{ stop: 1 }`
  - Fallback: Moonraker `PAUSE` / `RESUME` / `CANCEL_PRINT`

## Source of truth for behavior

Port logic from `scripts/iobroker-print-status.js` into `lib/` modules (e.g. `moonraker.js`, `crealityWs.js`, `cfs.js`) when scaffolding the adapter.
